    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 4, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Priya Ostrander, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Indication: Recurrent solid-food dysphagia; known peptic stricture of the distal esophagus."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "History: On June 4, 2026 the stricture was dilated over a guidewire with bougies to 15 mm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "Procedure: The gastroscope was advanced to the second portion of the duodenum."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "- Distal esophagus: a smooth, benign-appearing stricture at 37 cm, about 12 mm in diameter."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "- Today the stricture was dilated with a through-the-scope balloon to 16.5 mm and then 18 mm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "1. Recurrent peptic stricture of the distal esophagus, dilated today with a balloon to 18 mm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "Clinic follow-up in 8 weeks."
    }
